  "title": "Tawantinsuyu (Inca Empire)",
  "summary": "Tawantinsuyu, the Inca Empire, ruled much of the South American Andes in the 15th and 16th centuries from Cusco. It was linked by a road network of some 30,000 km whose four main routes began at Cusco's central square. Spanish forces took Cusco in 1533.",
